# kbdlight.manifest — config owned by mod_kbdlight (keyboard backlight).
#
# Three layers, two of them tracked here (update-system.md phase 2):
#   • /usr/share/w/defaults/kbdlight.conf + .schema — W's defaults and WHO may set
#     each key. Shipped data, class managed: W owns them, every update overwrites.
#   • /etc/w/kbdlight.conf — the admin's DEVIATIONS from those defaults. Class
#     override: the update never touches it; `w-reset kbdlight` drops the
#     deviations so the machine falls back to the vendor layer.
#
# NOT tracked here — generated output, regenerate with `sudo apply.sh --kbdlight`:
#   • the `w-kbdlight` entry in /etc/mkinitcpio.conf's HOOKS array
#   • /etc/w/kbdlight.boot + /etc/w/kbdlight.modules INSIDE the initramfs (build-
#     time snapshots written by the install hook; they do not exist on the running
#     system, only in the image)
# ~/.config/w/kbdlight.conf holds only the per-user key step, created on demand
# with no vendor default — class user-conf: `w-reset kbdlight` deletes it.
#
# Format: <path>\t<class>   class: managed | override | user-conf
/usr/share/w/defaults/kbdlight.conf	managed
/usr/share/w/defaults/kbdlight.schema	managed
/etc/w/kbdlight.conf	override
.config/w/kbdlight.conf	user-conf
